    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know, i know people say it gets better... but it doesn't feel like \"finding myself\" or anything like that. it just feels like i'm a hollow shell. like the person who actually lived, loved, and mattered part of me just died when they left. now i'm just this leftover trace of a person. it's hard to even bother with \"navigating\" something when there's nothing left to navigate.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The feeling that a deep part of your self is gone when someone you loved leaves is a profound and heartbreaking reality, one that \"just getting better\" often fails to acknowledge. It is completely understandable to feel like a hollow shell when the daily \"narrative\" of life with them no longer exists for you. Please try to be gentle with yourself as you let the emptiness be without trying to \"navigate\" a future that might not help until the grief eases.",
      "source": "target",
